Z||000000||Master_Sushi||10-22-2001||12:35 AM||||Hey, I was in canada this weekend and saw a few fieros. I  was heading to toronto on the highway. I think somewhat around the Guelph area I saw a stock looking silver fiero. It was an 85-86 with the bumper pads I beleave. I was kind of in a hurry and passed it at about 75-85mph in the left lane. I did beep at it though.<BR>Also saw a a gold SE around mississauga area.<P>Were any of these ppl from the forum??? Be interesting to see if it was.<P>I'm going to have to get to one of the canadian fiero meets some time. I'm often in the great white north   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P><BR>Thanks<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||Brandon86SE||10-22-2001||01:09 AM||||Wow!  Imagine!  Fiero's in Canada, I never would have imagined.  Must suck having to drive in snow all the time, wonder if any of 'em know how much fun they are on dry pavement?  Grinthock must, he just went down to PA for a meeting.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>anyway, that's enough of that!  lol<P>Yes, you should get up to one of our meetings!  I'd like to get down to the East sometime on a roadtrip and maybe check out one of the Ontario club's meetings too, or even to the US.  But that's long-term....<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||x-thumpr-x||10-22-2001||05:27 PM||||Well, GTA club has there next meeting on Nov 20 if you'd like to show up. I'm sure one of us can give you directions. <BR>As for snow, been there done that. Easy to drive the 4 banger in it. I just don't trust all the orientals and cabbies around here. I stick to TTC for the winter. <BR>Where about in Calgary Brandon? Last time I was out there, stayed with my uncle for a bit my some man-made lake near the south end of the Deerfoot trail. Couldn't remeber the name of the lake if my life depended on it, 8 years ago. Was thinking of going out there next summer after the Michigan show to visit relatives.<P><P>------------------<BR> Where there's a Willie, there's a way!<BR>red 84 coupe<BR>white 85GT<BR>black 85GT <BR>Willie..||||reg||1
Z||000003||Brandon86SE||10-22-2001||05:47 PM||||I live in SE Calgary, awfully close to the lake you mention (the one in McKenzie town I'm guessing by your description)  If you're out this way, try to make it to one of our meetings.  I haven't been able to get to as many as I would like (tend to work Thursday nights) but they are a great time, and I do try to get into all the big events.<P>Brandon||||reg||1
